<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130"><tei:pb n="474" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n498_medium.jpg"/><tei:head xml:lang="en">Psalm 130</tei:head><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/1"/>A Pilgrim Song. Out of the depths I call to thee, O Lord. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/2"/>O Lord, hear my voice; let thy ears be attentive to my supplicating voice. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/3"/>If thou, O Lord, shouldst keep strict account of iniquities, O Lord, who could live on? <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/4"/>But with thee there is forgiveness, that thou mayest be revered. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/5"/>I look for the Lord, my whole being hopes; I wait for his word. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/6"/>My soul waits for the Lord more eagerly than watchmen for the dawn, than watchmen for the dawn. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/7"/>O Israel, put your hope in the Lord; for with the Lord there is kindness; with him there is great saving power. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/130/8"/>It is he who will redeem Israel from all its iniquities. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
    </tei:body>
